<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine reconciliation by Codex, reused non-author of both current originals. Springtime and wintertime are established whole seasonal terms, without subword members. Each co-acting modifier owns contributing inside its own contributing-factor compound. The two complete la brten nas dependence phrases own Based on; covered nas is not separately nulled. Four active agentives have no separate English exponent. Each byas pa owns the second or fourth provides; first and third provides are reprises of the shared predicates. Four reg bya occurrences and the two body/consciousness member groups retain their distinct owners. Nominal experience syntax, anaphoric spirit subjects, rays/body expansions and the closing causal framing remain distributed and unwrapped. C15/C18 omit of before cold; C05 preserves it. No source wording or hgm_gloss is changed.</div>
<h2>Segment 272 &mdash; a cited verse on seasonal sensations</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s272S"><span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s272r1">de ltar</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w2">skye ba</span> yin te, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w3"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s272m4">bshes</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s272m5">spring</span></span> <span class="u case" data-d="6" data-l="s272p6">las</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w7">yi dvags</span> <span class="u number" data-d="6" data-l="s272p8">rnams</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s272p9">la</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w10">sos ka</span>&#x27;i dus <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s272p11">su</span> <span class="u topic" data-d="6" data-l="s272p12">ni</span>, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w13">zla ba</span>&#x27;ang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w14">tsha</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s272p15">la</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w16">dgun</span> <span class="u topic" data-d="6" data-l="s272p17">ni</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w18">nyi ma</span>&#x27;ang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w19">grang</span> , zhes <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w20">gsungs</span> pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s272p21">phyir</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s272S">It is a fact that they <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w2">get</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s272r1">this kind of</span> sensation, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s272p21">for</span> [Arya Nagarjuna&#x27;s] <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w3"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s272m5">Letter</span> to a <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s272m4">Friend</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w20">states</span>: <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s272p9">For</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w7">craving spirits</span>, even the light of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w13">moon</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s272p11">In</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w10">spring</span> is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w14">hot</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s272p15">and</span> even the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w16">winter</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w18">sun</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s272w19">cold</span>.<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s272p6"><span class="nul">Source ablative las: attribution uses the title as subject of states, with no separate from/in word.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s272p8"><span class="nul">Plural rnams is grammatically fused into the plural noun spirits; no separate English word is available, and its meaning is not claimed absent.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s272p12"><span class="nul">Topic ni has no separate English topic-marker word in this verse line.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s272p17"><span class="nul">Second topic ni has no separate topic-marker word in the English winter clause.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine reconciliation by Codex, reused non-author of both current originals. Letter to a Friend is the established title; its bracketed author is explanatory, with Friend and Letter as its only members. Plural rnams is fused into spirits; source las and two topic ni have no separate English word. Bound 'ang twice has overt even counterparts but no defensible compound parent containing them without supplied wording, so both are omitted, never nulled. The assertion and sensation reprises stay unwrapped. Capital For/In and lowercase causal for retain distinct owners. ILL:2342, physical label [2337], says summer; C05 says spring, positively attested in HTG2016. This difference does not establish a correction. No source wording or hgm_gloss is changed.</div>
<h2>Segment 273 &mdash; particular conditions and covered space</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s273S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w1">de</span> yang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w2">yul</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w3">dus</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w4">khyad par can</span> de dag gi <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s273r5">dbang gis skye ba</span> yin gyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w6">spyir</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s273r7">de ltar</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w8">skye ba</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w9">ma</span> yin te, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w10">nyi ma</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w11">steng du</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w12">grang ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w13">reg bya</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s273p14">yang</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w15">med</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w16">zla ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w17">steng du</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w18">tsha ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w19">reg bya</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s273p20">yang</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w21">med</span> pa&#x27;i phyir, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s273qfact">der thal</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w23">nyi ma</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w24">steng du</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w25">mun pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w26">rdzas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w27">med</span> pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s273p28">phyir</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s273S">All of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w1">this</span> is <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s273r5">caused by</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w4">extraordinary</span> circumstances of the particular <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w3">time</span> and <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w2">place</span>, for <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w6">generally speaking</span> it <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w9">never</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w8">happens</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s273r7">this way</span>: there is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w15">nothing</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s273p14">at all</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w11">about</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w10">sun</span> that can <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w13">feel</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w12">cold</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s273p20">and</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w21">nothing</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w17">about</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w16">moon</span> that can <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w19">feel</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w18">hot</span>. <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s273qfact">This too is a fact</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s273p28">for</span> there does <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w27">not exist</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w24">on</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w23">sun</span> any case of that <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w26">substance</span> we call &quot;<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s273w25">covered space</span>.&quot;</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine reconciliation by Codex, reused non-author of both current originals. The complete causal-arising phrase dbang gis skye ba owns caused by; no isolated skye ba/caused dictionary claim is made. Generally speaking and about/about/on are established lexical renderings. The complete der thal formula owns This too is a fact at phrase depth. The two negative-scope yang occurrences own at all and the clause-joining and; the initial topic yang and time/place conjunction stay unwrapped. Three med predicates own their separate nothing/nothing/not exist. Covered space is positively attested in HTG2016; comparative darkness does not justify changing it. Supplied participants, modal can, articles and naming language remain unwrapped. No source wording or hgm_gloss is changed. The first phyir and first for stay unwrapped because the concrete grounds are reorganized through the English colon; final phyir owns the second for. This distributed causal restructuring does not assert absence of meaning.</div>
